#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/@taon-dev/docs/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/kv-repositories.component.html:2
msgid "Taon KV repositories provide typed key-value storage through injectable repositories. The API is inspired by key-value systems such as Redis and Cloudflare Workers KV, with a document-oriented approach to storing structured values similar to MongoDB. These comparisons describe the design inspiration. The examples below use Taon’s repository API."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/@taon-dev/docs/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/kv-repositories.component.html:3
msgid "Use a KV repository when you read or replace a value by a known key, such as application settings or a cached snapshot. Call the repository from backend code. Browser UI code should access the data through a Taon API endpoint."
msgstr ""

